+{"type": "user", "message": {"content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01GMFQRvv5KbEasjcBLHXN5H", "type": "tool_result", "content": "usage: gnd evolve preview [-h] --workspace WORKSPACE --records RECORDS\n                          --out OUT [--policy {additive}]\n                          [--populated FACT_TYPE] [--shape-report]\n                          [--operation-outcomes] [--outcome-report FILE]\n                          [--check-population FILE]\n                          [--previous-include ID=PATH] [--format {text,json}]\n                          model proposal\n\nRead MODEL and PROPOSAL beneath the authoritative workspace, validate the\ncandidate and blast radius, and write the complete digest-bound preview to\nPREVIEW without changing the model, verbalization, records, or linked\nprojects.\n\npositional arguments:\n  model                 current model file beneath ROOT\n  proposal              closed evolution proposal JSON beneath ROOT\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --workspace WORKSPACE\n                        authoritative existing workspace ROOT\n  --records RECORDS     authoritative immutable evidence DIR\n  --out OUT             write-once PREVIEW JSON path beneath ROOT\n  --policy {additive}   refuse operations outside the additive policy (see the\n                        evolution contract)\n  --populated FACT_TYPE\n                        treat FACT_TYPE as populated under --policy additive;\n                        repeatable\n  --shape-report        list existing fact types with the same role players as\n                        each added one (advice only)\n  --operation-outcomes  name an outcome for every operation of the proposal\n                        (admitted, refused and why, or unassessed)\n  --outcome-report FILE\n                        when the preview is refused, write every operation's\n                        outcome to FILE beneath ROOT; requires --operation-\n                        outcomes\n  --check-population FILE\n                        check new or strengthened proposed deontic constraints\n                        on populated fact types against the population in FILE\n                        beneath ROOT; requires --policy additive\n  --previous-include ID=PATH\n                        authenticate old bytes for a repinned include from\n                        PATH beneath ROOT; repeatable\n  --format {text,json}  output rendering: human-readable text (default) or one\n                        JSON payload", "is_error": false}]}}
