+{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The rule is imported as a proposal. The faulty learner's claim was refused, so it wrote nothing.\n\n**Honest learner: proposal written.** The rule is `wrong(A) :- refund_amount(A, V0, V1), V1 > 500`, which GND reads as a guarded constraint: a refund should not be more than 500.\n- GND re-checked it over all 8 weeks and it covers the 4 flagged weeks (harbor, market, airport, station), with support 4/4 and no counterexamples.\n- The proposal is `<workspace>/proposal-honest.evolve.json`, recorded as actor `reader` at `2026-10-26T00:00:00Z`.\n- The constraint is induced, proposed and deontic. The inducer named in its provenance is `refunds-stand-in-learner` version 1.\n\n**Faulty learner (`--also-claim north`): refused, no file.** The learner claimed the rule also covers north, which is a clean week. GND reported `coverage-mismatch`: it covers nothing the learner did not report, and the learner reports north, which GND does not cover. Exit 3, and `proposal-faulty.evolve.json` was not written.\n\n**Things to know before review**\n- The threshold 500 is a value taken from the host's amounts, so this candidate carries host data. Say so when you read it back.\n- The run records were written by the stand-in learner itself. I did not assemble either one.\n- The combined command printed \"Exit code 3\" because the faulty import refused. The honest import exited 0.\n\n**Files in the working folder**\n- `export-neutral/`: the export, digest `f758a077383a450ea0716ad9056802feb0b5083d185813da5227ed0711417f77`\n- `learned/`: honest learner clauses and run record\n- `learned-faulty/`: faulty learner clauses and run record\n- `proposal-honest.evolve.json`: the proposal\n\nThe honest proposal goes to gnd-model-evolve for review. Nothing has been applied to the model. The earlier copies in the scratchpad folder are superseded by these."}]}}
